# What `vercel deploy` must not upload.
#
# The CLI uploads the working directory, not the git tree, so .gitignore does
# not apply here — anything left out has to be named again. Two of these are
# not merely wasteful:
#
#   .env*      `vercel link` writes .env.local with a VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN in it,
#              and `vercel env pull` fills the same file with real project
#              secrets. Uploading a credential back to the deployment that
#              issued it is not a disaster, but there is no reason to.
#   _gpx/      ~25 MB of raw GPX exports. Jekyll never builds them (underscore
#              prefix) and /hikes/ is built from them ahead of time, so they
#              would be uploaded on every deploy to be ignored on arrival.
.env*
_gpx/

# Build products and local installs. Vercel makes its own.
_site/
.jekyll-cache/
.sass-cache/
vendor/
node_modules/
